<title>GERMANY: TABLE - West German June ind. output rises 0.4 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - West German June ind. output rises 0.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following indicator (previously-announced data in brackets):</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT   June 97	  May 97     June 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +0.4	 -1.1 (-0.4)   +0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +0.9	 +0.7 (+1.8)   -0.3</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		96.5	 96.1 (97.1)   95.6</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				    June 97		  May 97</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining		     86.0	 +2.5     83.9	 -8.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   96.1	 +0.1     96.0	 -0.8</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods  101.1	 -0.3    101.4	 -0.6</p>
<p>	Capital goods     97.8	 +1.9     96.0	 -1.4</p>
<p>	Consumer durables 82.9	 +3.9     79.8	 -4.2</p>
<p>	Consumer goods    87.9	 -3.5     91.1	 +0.8</p>
<p> Energy output	   107.8	 -3.0    111.1	 +3.0</p>
<p> Construction	     94.7	 +7.4     88.2	 -7.4</p>
<p>Two month comparison May/Jun 97 with Mar/Apr 97:</p>
<p>    Industrial production	    -1.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison May/Jun 97 with Mar/Apr 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +0.8</p>
<p> Mining				    -1.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +1.9</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods     +4.1</p>
<p>		Capital goods	    +3.7</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	-2.5</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	   -4.6</p>
<p> Energy output			   -0.8</p>
<p> Construction			    -8.2</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 260 97 150</p>
</text>
